:/tmp/datalad_temp_tree_test_run_inputs_outputsv3qpxcvo [origin]'}]\n```\nand of cause manual re-get worked out\n```\nroot@smaug:/tmp/buildd/datalad-0.11.8# cd /tmp/datalad_temp_test_run_inputs_outputsqm9a569m\nroot@smaug:/tmp/datalad_temp_test_run_inputs_outputsqm9a569m# git annex get /tmp/datalad_temp_test_run_inputs_outputsqm9a569m/c.txt\nget c.txt (from origin...) \nMD5E-s5--d394994e9541622e8018542d886abaa8.txt\n              5 100%    0.00kB/s    0:00:00 (xfr#1, to-chk=0/1)\n(checksum...) ok\n(recording state in git...)\nroot@smaug:/tmp/datalad_temp_test_run_inputs_outputsqm9a569m# cat .git/config \n[core]\n        repositoryformatversion = 0\n        filemode = true\n        bare = false\n        logallrefupdates = true\n[remote \"origin\"]\n        url = /tmp/datalad_temp_tree_test_run_inputs_outputsv3qpxcvo\n        fetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*\n        annex-uuid = 088cedcc-a08e-4ab4-8a64-d72785630c37\n...\n```\nso it does smell like some racing in git-annex (attn @joeyh )","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1573591610,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1MzEwNjcyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3653#issuecomment-553106728"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e [{'type': 'file', 'refds': '/tmp/datalad_temp_test_run_inputs_outputsqm9a569m', 'status': 'error', 'path': '/tmp/datalad_temp_test_run_inputs_outputsqm9a569m/c.txt', 'action': 'get', 'annexkey': 'MD5E-s5--d394994e9541622e8018542d886abaa8.txt', 'message': 'transfer already in progress, or unable to take transfer lock; Unable to access these remotes: origin; Try making some of these repositories available:; \\t088cedcc-a08e-4ab4-8a64-d72785630c37 -- root@smaug:/tmp/datalad_temp_tree_test_run_inputs_outputsv3qpxcvo [origin]'}]\n\n\u003e so it does smell like some racing in git-annex (attn @joeyh )\n\nEither multiple threads or multiple processes have tried to download the\nsame key concurrently. This is very easy to reproduce, just start a get\nand run it again in another terminal.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1573595641,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1MzEzMzY3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3653#issuecomment-553133679"},"message":"hm... I will try to dig out more, but :\n\n- my initial hint on that it could be the same key was wrong (so there would be transfer from it from multiple threads) -- then seems to fail differently https://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/parallel_get_to_the_files_for_the_same_key_would_fail_with__thread_blocked_indefinitely_in_an_STM_transaction/?updated\n- it feels that it is something to be addressed at git annex level one way or another.   message is too ambiguous (is it about transfer? or unable to acquire a lock? or actually cannot access remote?) . If transfer is in progress -- annex imho should wait (with some time out) until transfer completes.  If lock is not available -- wait for it (with some timeout) to become available and verify if transfer is needed. Time out might be even very long if from lock information it knows that it is some other live git-annex process on the same box.  And it is not that `origin` was not available here (it was) so it shouldn't complain about that here.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1573662367,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1MzQ3OTI0NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3653#issuecomment-553479244"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e hm... I will try to dig out more, but :\n\u003e \n\u003e   • my initial hint on that it could be the same key was wrong (so there would\n\u003e     be transfer from it from multiple threads) -- then seems to fail\n\u003e     differently https://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/\n\u003e     parallel_get_to_the_files_for_the_same_key_would_fail_with__thread_blocked_indefinitely_in_an_STM_transaction\n\u003e     /?updated\n\nBut that's a closed bug report from 2017. The current behavior if two threads\nboth try to transfer the same key would be the same as what you showed.\n\n\u003e   • it feels that it is something to be addressed at git annex level one way or\n\u003e     another. message is too ambiguous (is it about transfer? or unable to\n\u003e     acquire a lock? or actually cannot access remote?\n\nThe message is \"transfer already in progress, or unable to take transfer\nlock\". There's a later, more general error message displayed at a higher\nlevel. (I don't know what is making them be separated by \"; \" , it does not\nseem to be done by git-annex.)\n\n\u003e If transfer is in\n\u003e progress -- annex imho should wait (with some time out) until transfer\n\u003e completes. If lock is not available -- wait for it (with some timeout)\n\nThis has been discussed before, I think even between us. Waiting will\ncause git-annex to block if another git-annex, running a transfer, is\nsuspended, or has been blocked. A timeout gets right back to the current\nbehavior, so there's no guarantee that a failure can't happen due to\nanother process running the transfer.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1573662459,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1MzQ3OTk1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3653#issuecomment-553479951"},"message":"Joey Hess wrote:\n\u003e But that's a closed bug report from 2017. The current behavior if two threads\n\u003e both try to transfer the same key would be the same as what you showed.\n\nNm, I thought you meant a different bug report, not the one you just\nopened.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null}]}